              "size_meaning": "n = number of dot‑separated items in *each* of the three components (interpreters, ABIs, platforms).  The tag length grows roughly as 3·n and the number of generated Tag objects grows as n³, which makes the old implementation repeatedly split strings.",
              "make_source": "def make(n):\n    # build n interpreters, n ABIs, n platforms\n    interps = '.'.join(f'py{i}' for i in range(1, n+1))\n    abis = '.'.join(f'abi{i}' for i in range(1, n+1))\n    plats = '.'.join(f'plat{i}' for i in range(1, n+1))\n    tag = f'{interps}-{abis}-{plats}'\n    return [[tag]]",
